# fresh_resume_version_f5_control: A rvg_device_will_resume refused at the capability check (a device-info key 1 of 0xffffffff: IncompatibleDevice, 4) has already set the binary version from the blob: on a device the guest never versioned, 0x1034 then reads 0xf5, and a later suspend's blob carries key 2 = 0xf5. A new process resumes that blob as a guest of version 0xf5. The control, with no failed resume first, carries 0.
{"op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
{"label": "a fresh device", "off": "0x1034", "op": "mmio_r"}
{"name": "willSuspend", "op": "api"}
{"name": "finishSuspend", "op": "api", "slot": "s"}
{"image": "0", "op": "handoff_save"}
{"op": "phase"}
{"handoff_load": {"image": "0"}, "op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
{"name": "willResume", "op": "api", "slot": "s"}
{"name": "didResume", "op": "api"}
{"op": "quiesce", "quiet_ms": 100}
{"label": "resumed", "op": "events"}
{"from": "0x1000", "label": "registers", "op": "mmio_sweep", "step": 4, "to": "0x1040"}
